                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15001762" author="gauravkumar37" created="Thu, 12 Nov 2015 06:47:25 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks for filing the issue.&lt;br/&gt;
Should the contents be wrapped within the parent container or should there be a scrollable div holding the results when they are wide enough. Having a scrollable div could also mean we could opt for both vertical and horizontal scrollbars, similar to what Jupyter does for long results.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15001769" author="corneadoug" created="Thu, 12 Nov 2015 06:57:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;There should be a scrollbar on both axis if the result content is bigger than the container.&lt;br/&gt;
We are not really supposed to have that problem with graphs (since they are 100%), but I do see it sometimes when resizing.&lt;br/&gt;
And it&apos;s already handled when results are in the table.&lt;br/&gt;
So the main use would be for custom HTML rendering&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15001858" author="gauravkumar37" created="Thu, 12 Nov 2015 08:49:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;It also happens when printing out statements to stdout from the code without using any HTML or other widgets.&lt;br/&gt;
E.g.:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;Seq(1 to 1000).foreach(print)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15006178" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 16 Nov 2015 03:01:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user corneadoug opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/436&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/incubator-zeppelin/pull/436&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-414&quot; title=&quot;Big Result are shown outside the container&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-414&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-414&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; - Contain result inside paragraph&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Taking care of &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-414&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-414&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    I only applied it on ``HTML`` and ``ANGULAR`` result, because it is the only one that i saw breaking.&lt;br/&gt;
    Didn&apos;t have any problem with other types, although I couldn&apos;t test with the response type ``IMG``, any good example to test it?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Here is how it looks now:&lt;br/&gt;
    !&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;screen shot 2015-11-16 at 11 54 47 am&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;a href=&quot;https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/710411/11173419/8d137ebe-8c59-11e5-924b-a7fcc43447cf.png&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/710411/11173419/8d137ebe-8c59-11e5-924b-a7fcc43447cf.png&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;


